{{ElectionsOK}}
The '''1996 United States Senate election in Oklahoma''' was held on November 5, 1996. Incumbent [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] U.S. Senator [[Jim Inhofe]], first elected in a [[1994 United States Senate special election in Oklahoma|1994 special election]], won re-election to his first full term. This election is the first time that a Republican was re-elected to the Class 2 Senate seat from Oklahoma.

